{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And if you do not listen to Me.</b> To be toiling in Torah, to know the midrash of the Sages. One might think: to the fulfillment of the commandments? When it says ״וְלֹא תַעֲשׂוּ״ and so forth — behold, fulfillment of commandments is stated. So how do I establish ״וְאִם לֹא תִּשְׁמְעוּ לִי״? To be toiling in Torah. And what does ״לִי״ tell me? I have only this: one who recognizes his Master and intends to rebel against Him. And so with Nimrod: ״גִּבּוֹר צַיִד לִפְנֵי יְהֹוָה״ (Genesis 10) — who recognizes Him and intends to rebel against Him. And so with the men of Sodom: ״רָעִים וְחַטָּאִים לַיְהֹוָה מְאֹד״ (ibid. 13) — who recognize their Master and intend to rebel against Him (Sifra)." "<b>And you do not do.</b> Because you do not study, you do not do — behold, two transgressions."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:08:39.654562946Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}